<title>UK: Compass shares rise on U.S. acquisition.</title>
<headline>Compass shares rise on U.S. acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Compass Group Plc rose six pence to 555 after the food service firm announced it acquired the dining and food service assets of Service America.</p>
<p>Kleinwort Benson said the assets were an excellent strategic fit and added that the acquisition would be modestly earnings enhancing. In a note, the broker said it raised its earnings estimates for the year to September 1997 to 31.0 pence per share from 30.0 pence.</p>
<p>Compass will pay 8.4 million stg in cash and issue 12.9 million in loan notes as well as 10.3 million shares at 5.73 stg to finance the deal.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
